## Source audit and change

- Java 5.5.1 Push retry and send-back paths dynamically call
  `MessageExt.getReconsumeTimes` and `setReconsumeTimes` on base-typed
  `MessageExt` values. Rust previously read and wrote the base field directly.
- Added optional getter/setter hooks to `MessageExtSubtype`. Base behavior is
  unchanged when a custom subtype leaves either hook at its default.
- Extended the invoked Java direct-consume subtype fixture: its setter records
  one write, its getter returns `13`, and the callback records that value.
  Rust checks the same callback data and setter count; all 27 direct-consume
  cases pass.
- Updated the Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 compatibility crosswalks and the
  release checklist. Other inherited virtual methods remain part of the broad
  audit.

